  "cover_link": "https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/marveldatabase/images/5/5f/Fantastic_Four_Annual_Vol_1_1.jpg",
  "plot_summary": "The second story in the annual is a re-telling of Spider-Man's first encounter with the FF, but <i>with additional detail</i>, apparently in response to \"countless requests\" to re-tell it, but devote more space.&nbsp; \"And so - because you requested it...\"&nbsp; The story is written by Stan Lee, drawn by Jack Kirby and inked by Steve Ditko, so all the players are involved here.&nbsp; (Though Kirby just doesn't seem to be able to get Spider-Man's mask right.&nbsp; Note the cover where it looks like a checkerboard pattern, as opposed to the way it looks on the Ditko-inked pages within.)\n\nIt's largely a true re-telling, with only additional battle panels, where Spider-Man takes on each FF member individually.&nbsp; Thus, I feel no need to give it its own rating, though I don't really see how it improves things much at all, except to give the reader a better sense of where Spider-Man ranks as a hero in his own right - very impressive encounters early in the young hero's career, but largely brings nothing new to the table.",
  "grade_one_liner": "FIXME - write something",
  "subtitle": "FIXME - write something",
  "review_text": "[SPAN: severity=info; fonttype=bold; text=FOR THE RECORD:]\n[BR] This is a review of the second of the three stories found in this magazine.\n[BR] My review on the first story is posted elsewhere.\n\n[DIVIDER]\n\nThe second story in the annual is a re-telling of Spider-Man's first encounter with the FF, but <i>with additional detail</i>, apparently in response to \"countless requests\" to re-tell it, but devote more space.&nbsp; \"And so - because you requested it...\"&nbsp; The story is written by Stan Lee, drawn by Jack Kirby and inked by Steve Ditko, so all the players are involved here.&nbsp; (Though Kirby just doesn't seem to be able to get Spider-Man's mask right.&nbsp; Note the cover where it looks like a checkerboard pattern, as opposed to the way it looks on the Ditko-inked pages within.)\n\n[BOTTOM_LINE]\nIt's largely a true re-telling, with only additional battle panels, where Spider-Man takes on each FF member individually.&nbsp; Thus, I feel no need to give it its own rating, though I don't really see how it improves things much at all, except to give the reader a better sense of where Spider-Man ranks as a hero in his own right - very impressive encounters early in the young hero's career, but largely brings nothing new to the table.",
  "highlight": "FIXME - write something"
}